00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:20.810
And you know that the
cloud in and of itself

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:22.547
is elastic and scalable,
but the key word

00:11:22.547 --> 00:11:25.130
that I want you to focus on for
today is that it's a platform.

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.940
It can be anything
that you want it to be,

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:29.030
so the key three
areas of the Cloud--

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:30.971
Compute, doing a lot
of computational power,

00:11:30.971 --> 00:11:32.720
so that you're running
a bunch of scripts,

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:33.695
or you're serving up
your applications,

00:11:33.695 --> 00:11:35.930
or you're performing
a lot of computation.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:38.090
Data and analytics,
that's my specialty.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:41.210
So if you are running analysis
over petabytes of data,

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:43.730
and you want it to be done
at a blazing fast speed,

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:45.560
and you don't want to
worry about the size

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:47.870
of your hard drive
limiting the amount of data

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:50.570
that you can store, the platform
can be used for that as well--

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:52.580
or if you wanted to get
into machine learning.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.121
And last but not
least, if you wanted

00:11:54.121 --> 00:11:55.820
to not worry about
load balancing

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.960
or any of these other
typical headaches

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:59.960
that comes with running
an entire infrastructure

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:02.060
